  "description_nl": "Part A from the client master; OtherInformation1 (the CA) from the CA firm's approved application; clause 18 (depreciation), 31(a) (loans accepted), 31(c) (repaid) and 23 (payments to persons in s.40A(2)(b)) from rows mapped '3CD <clause>'. clause_lists says which list each clause fills; skip_zero leaves out a row whose figure is nil there (a loan not repaid has no 31(b) line). The rest stays the schema's default for the department's utility. 2026-10-05 owner (3CD from a party master): main_amount: a row whose only amount sits under a title we cannot read still gives that amount; text_columns: the Yes/No and words a statement gives per party; also: a loan row repaid in the year is listed under 31(c) repayments too; party_clauses: the clauses whose rows name a party (for Fill the party master). 2026-10-05 owner (\"yes\" to the form's own numbering): repayments are clause 31(c), as Form 3CD numbers them; 31(b) is a specified sum taken (s.269SS) - Form3cdSec269SSDtls.",
